          "id": "PRR_kwDONtWm_c8AAAABCFVt0w",
          "databaseId": 4434783699,
          "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR appears to (partially) bring the kernel heap (`mm::heap`) under Verus verification by adding spec functions, `verifier::*` annotations, and external bodies—while noting verification is limited because `mm/frame` is not fully verified.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Exposes `ostd::mm::heap` publicly from `mm::mod`.\n- Adds Verus spec/ensures/requires scaffolding across heap slot, slab, and free-list code.\n- Adjusts heap allocator dispatch and abort paths for verification (including commenting out allocator wiring).\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 5 out of 5 changed files in this pull request and generated 5 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `ostd/src/mm/mod.rs` | Exports the `heap` module publicly. |\r\n| `ostd/src/mm/heap/mod.rs` | Adds Verus assumptions/specifications and changes allocator wiring/abort behavior. |\r\n| `ostd/src/mm/heap/slot.rs` | Adds spec helpers and proof obligations around slot info/addresses; large-slot APIs currently removed via comments. |\r\n| `ostd/src/mm/heap/slot_list.rs` | Wraps list logic in `verus!` and adds spec/external-body annotations. |\r\n| `ostd/src/mm/heap/slab.rs` | Introduces Verus modeling/representation for slab metadata; `Slab::new`/`dealloc` currently stubbed. |\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Comments suppressed due to low confidence (1)</summary>\n\n**ostd/src/mm/heap/mod.rs:124**\n* The `#[alloc_error_handler]` and `#[global_allocator]` definitions are now commented out. If `ostd::mm::heap` is intended to provide the dispatch-based global allocator, this effectively disables it and can break any code relying on heap allocation. If the goal is to avoid these items during verification, prefer `cfg(not(feature = \"verify\"))` gates over commenting them out so non-verify builds still get the allocator wiring.\n```\n/*\n#[alloc_error_handler]\nfn handle_alloc_error(layout: core::alloc::Layout) -> ! {\n    abort_with_message!(\"Heap allocation error, layout = {:#x?}\", layout);\n}\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/asterinas/vostd/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
          "bodyHTML": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">Pull request overview</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR appears to (partially) bring the kernel heap (<code class=\"notranslate\">mm::heap</code>) under Verus verification by adding spec functions, <code class=\"notranslate\">verifier::*</code> annotations, and external bodies—while noting verification is limited because <code class=\"notranslate\">mm/frame</code> is not fully verified.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Changes:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Exposes <code class=\"notranslate\">ostd::mm::heap</code> publicly from <code class=\"notranslate\">mm::mod</code>.</li>\n<li>Adds Verus spec/ensures/requires scaffolding across heap slot, slab, and free-list code.</li>\n<li>Adjusts heap allocator dispatch and abort paths for verification (including commenting out allocator wiring).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Reviewed changes</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Copilot reviewed 5 out of 5 changed files in this pull request and generated 5 comments.</p>\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\"table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>File</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">ostd/src/mm/mod.rs</code></td>\n<td>Exports the <code class=\"notranslate\">heap</code> module publicly.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">ostd/src/mm/heap/mod.rs</code></td>\n<td>Adds Verus assumptions/specifications and changes allocator wiring/abort behavior.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">ostd/src/mm/heap/slot.rs</code></td>\n<td>Adds spec helpers and proof obligations around slot info/addresses; large-slot APIs currently removed via comments.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">ostd/src/mm/heap/slot_list.rs</code></td>\n<td>Wraps list logic in <code class=\"notranslate\">verus!</code> and adds spec/external-body annotations.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">ostd/src/mm/heap/slab.rs</code></td>\n<td>Introduces Verus modeling/representation for slab metadata; <code class=\"notranslate\">Slab::new</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">dealloc</code> currently stubbed.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Comments suppressed due to low confidence (1)</summary>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>ostd/src/mm/heap/mod.rs:124</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">#[alloc_error_handler]</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">#[global_allocator]</code> definitions are now commented out. If <code class=\"notranslate\">ostd::mm::heap</code> is intended to provide the dispatch-based global allocator, this effectively disables it and can break any code relying on heap allocation. If the goal is to avoid these items during verification, prefer <code class=\"notranslate\">cfg(not(feature = \"verify\"))</code> gates over commenting them out so non-verify builds still get the allocator wiring.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"/*\n#[alloc_error_handler]\nfn handle_alloc_error(layout: core::alloc::Layout) -&gt; ! {\n    abort_with_message!(&quot;Heap allocation error, layout = {:#x?}&quot;, layout);\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">/*\n#[alloc_error_handler]\nfn handle_alloc_error(layout: core::alloc::Layout) -&gt; ! {\n    abort_with_message!(\"Heap allocation error, layout = {:#x?}\", layout);\n}\n</code></pre></div>\n</details>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">💡 <a href=\"/asterinas/vostd/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\">Learn how to get started</a>.</p>",
