      "body": "`mm::heap` is now exported unconditionally, but the heap implementation in this PR is verification-stubbed (e.g. `Slab::new` always returns `Err(NoMemory)`, and `HeapSlot::alloc_large`/`dealloc_large` are commented out). Exposing the module like this makes it easy for non-verification builds/consumers to accidentally depend on a non-functional heap API. Consider gating the module behind the `verify` feature (or otherwise ensuring the exec implementation remains functional when `heap` is public).",
      "created_at": "2026-06-05T08:24:15Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-05T08:24:17Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/asterinas/vostd/pull/505#discussion_r3361399035",
      "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/asterinas/vostd/pulls/505",
