      "body_html": "<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">mm::heap</code> is now exported unconditionally, but the heap implementation in this PR is verification-stubbed (e.g. <code class=\"notranslate\">Slab::new</code> always returns <code class=\"notranslate\">Err(NoMemory)</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">HeapSlot::alloc_large</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">dealloc_large</code> are commented out). Exposing the module like this makes it easy for non-verification builds/consumers to accidentally depend on a non-functional heap API. Consider gating the module behind the <code class=\"notranslate\">verify</code> feature (or otherwise ensuring the exec implementation remains functional when <code class=\"notranslate\">heap</code> is public).</p>",
      "body_text": "mm::heap is now exported unconditionally, but the heap implementation in this PR is verification-stubbed (e.g. Slab::new always returns Err(NoMemory), and HeapSlot::alloc_large/dealloc_large are commented out). Exposing the module like this makes it easy for non-verification builds/consumers to accidentally depend on a non-functional heap API. Consider gating the module behind the verify feature (or otherwise ensuring the exec implementation remains functional when heap is public).",
