      "body": "`Slab::new` is currently hardcoded to `Err(NoMemory)` (with the real allocation logic commented out). This makes the slab allocator unusable and breaks downstream users that expect `Slab::new()` to allocate (e.g. the OSDK heap allocator calls `Slab::new()` in `osdk/deps/heap-allocator/src/slab_cache.rs`). If this is only to unblock proof work, consider `#[cfg(feature=\"verify\")]` stubbing while keeping the exec implementation intact for non-verify builds.",
      "created_at": "2026-06-05T08:24:16Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-05T08:24:17Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/asterinas/vostd/pull/505#discussion_r3361399135",
