        }
      },
      "body_html": "<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Slab::new</code> is currently hardcoded to <code class=\"notranslate\">Err(NoMemory)</code> (with the real allocation logic commented out). This makes the slab allocator unusable and breaks downstream users that expect <code class=\"notranslate\">Slab::new()</code> to allocate (e.g. the OSDK heap allocator calls <code class=\"notranslate\">Slab::new()</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">osdk/deps/heap-allocator/src/slab_cache.rs</code>). If this is only to unblock proof work, consider <code class=\"notranslate\">#[cfg(feature=\"verify\")]</code> stubbing while keeping the exec implementation intact for non-verify builds.</p>",
      "body_text": "Slab::new is currently hardcoded to Err(NoMemory) (with the real allocation logic commented out). This makes the slab allocator unusable and breaks downstream users that expect Slab::new() to allocate (e.g. the OSDK heap allocator calls Slab::new() in osdk/deps/heap-allocator/src/slab_cache.rs). If this is only to unblock proof work, consider #[cfg(feature=\"verify\")] stubbing while keeping the exec implementation intact for non-verify builds.",
